      "role": "user",
      "content": "yeah, redundancy makes a lot of sense. i guess i'm just stuck on the idea of those \"glitches\" you mentioned. it's almost like there's a tiny, invisible force or some sort of chaos factor that just wants to see things break. do you think there's ever a case where a structure's failure is actually caused by something totally mischievous or disruptive that isn't just a physical property like fatigue or soil settling? like, something that feels more like a deliberate little sabotage rather than just bad luck?",
      "source": "evaluator"
